when LLM fails. | File created automatically by `main.py`. |\n\n---\n\n**4. Model Knowledge (Technical & Architectural Details)**\n\n| Area | Specifics |\n|------|-----------|\n| **Package layout** (`lead_enrichment`):<br>‑ `main.py` – CLI entry point, async orchestration, uses `run_domain`.<br>‑ `crawler.py` – async HTTP fetcher using `httpx`, `fetch_page(url)` (30 s timeout), `discover_subpages(base_url)` (HEAD checks for common paths), `process_domain(domain)` (aggregates cleaned markdown).<br>‑ `processor.py` – `clean_html(html)` strips `<script>`, `<style>`, navigation/footer selectors, then converts to markdown via `html2text`.<br>‑ `models.py` – Pydantic `Leader` and `CompanyInfo` schemas (exact fields required by assignment).<br>‑ `llm.py` – `BaseLLM` abstract class; `OpenAIClient` (legacy `openai.ChatCompletion.create`) with `extract_info` building a system + user prompt, truncating content to ~12 k chars, parsing JSON response, logging token usage via `utils.log_token_usage`.<br>‑ `config.py` – loads `.env` (project root) using `python-dotenv`; provides dict with `llm_provider`, `openai_api_key`, etc.<br>‑ `utils.py` – `retry_async` decorator (exponential back‑off), `log_token_usage` (writes JSONL entries). |\n| **Async flow**: `main_async` creates a single `llm_client` (shared across domains), then spawns `run_domain` coroutines for each domain via `asyncio.gather`. Each `run_domain` calls `process_domain` (crawler) → `llm_client.extract_info` (LLM) → returns either parsed `CompanyInfo` dict or placeholder. |\n| **Error handling**: All network or LLM failures are caught; warnings logged; placeholder returned with `confidence_score = 0.0`. This satisfies the “never crash” requirement. |\n| **Dependency quirks**: `openai==0.28` works synchronously; we wrap the call with `asyncio.to_thread`. The newer `openai>=1.0` API caused `APIRemovedInV1` errors, hence the downgrade. |\n| **Rate‑limit / credit issue**: The provided OpenAI key returned `RateLimitError: credit_balance_exhausted`. The client propagates the exception, which is caught in `run_domain` → placeholder returned. |\n| **Redirect handling**: `httpx.AsyncClient` follows redirects by default, but HEAD checks for common sub‑paths returned `301` for `postman.com`. Those URLs were **not** added to `subpages` (only 200 OK are kept). The homepage fetch (`https://postman.com`) also follows redirects; however the request timed out (seen in logs) and resulted in “No content extracted”. |\n| **Token logging**: `utils.log_token_usage` writes per‑domain entries to `token_log.jsonl` (not yet examined). |\n| **Configuration loading**: `config.load_config()` searches for `.env` two directories up from the module file (project root). Both a root `.env` and a `lead_enrichment/.env` exist with the same key; the loader will pick the first found (project root). |\n| **Testing / verification**: No automated tests were added; manual run verified that the script executes and writes `output.json`. |\n\n---\n\n**5. Files and Code**\n\n| Path (absolute) | Action | Summary of Change / Reason |\n|------------------|--------|----------------------------|\n| `C:\\Users\\new\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\4fdbd629-b1b9-4bee-a13c-8876484f2243\\lead_enrichment\\__init__.py` | Created | Package initializer (empty). |\n| `C:\\Users\\new\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\4fdbd629-b1b9-4bee-a13c-8876484f2243\\lead_enrichment\\main.py` | Created / Overwritten | CLI entry point with robust placeholder fallback logic. |\n| `C:\\Users\\new\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\4fdbd629-b1b9-4bee-a13c-8876484f2243\\lead_enrichment\\crawler.py` | Created / Overwritten (twice) | Final version uses `httpx` for async GET/HEAD, includes retry decorator, 30 s timeout, and returns concatenated cleaned markdown. |\n| `C:\\Users\\new\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\4fdbd629-b1b9-4bee-a13c-8876484f2243\\lead_enrichment\\processor.py` | Created | Strips scripts, styles, navigation/footer, converts HTML → markdown. |\n| `C:\\Use